An ant’s main purpose is to help its **colony survive and reproduce**: workers gather food, care for the young, build and defend the nest, and support the queen and brood[20]. In nature, ants also play important roles by **aerating soil, recycling nutrients, dispersing seeds, and controlling pests**[1][5][18].
